  "objects": [
    {
      "kind": "sign",
      "x": 16,
      "y": 2,
      "text": [
        "TIDEGLASS. Thirty-one thousand, and a hundred and four of them harbour pilots.",
        "Gate Avenue south to the Tide Hall. The Parade crosses it. Everything else runs downhill.",
        "Somebody has scratched under it: EVENTUALLY EVERYTHING RUNS DOWNHILL"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "sign",
      "x": 12,
      "y": 9,
      "text": [
        "NETMAKERS ROW. Lodgings, four hundred and twelve rooms, none of them free.",
        "The board underneath lists work going on the boats. Half the cards are two seasons old."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "sign",
      "x": 19,
      "y": 16,
      "text": [
        "THE TIDE HALL. Keeper Marit Vane.",
        "The challenge is fought down in the works, in water, and you go in wet or not at all."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "sign",
      "x": 28,
      "y": 22,
      "text": [
        "THE PARADE. Stores both sides, from the west wall to the Foundation gate.",
        "Carts keep left. Barrows keep left. Everyone keeps left.",
        "Nobody keeps left."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "sign",
      "x": 10,
      "y": 26,
      "text": [
        "KIN CLINIC. Open, always. The bunks upstairs are free this season.",
        "A card in the window: NO, WE STILL DO NOT KNOW WHY THE FISH LEFT."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "sign",
      "x": 18,
      "y": 26,
      "text": [
        "TIDEGLASS PROVISIONER. Oilskin, line, tonic, vessels.",
        "Prices rose in the spring and the sign explaining why has been taken down twice."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "sign",
      "x": 9,
      "y": 32,
      "text": [
        "THE CUT. Dug by hand in the year of the long frost so the market could load off the water.",
        "Deep enough for a punt. Shallow enough to walk, if you know how."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "sign",
      "x": 22,
      "y": 38,
      "text": [
        "OLD HARBOUR. The oldest stone in Tideglass and the least of the money.",
        "Fish market under the long roof. Auction at four. Do not be late; do not be early either."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "sign",
      "x": 18,
      "y": 46,
      "text": [
        "HARBOUR FRONT. West mole and the light that way. Dockyards and the yards east.",
        "Slack water is at seven. It has been at seven for three weeks, which is not how tides work."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "sign",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 20,
      "text": [
        "THE GLASSRUN. Cut from the north wall to the harbour, and the reason the city is here.",
        "Barges have right of way. So does the water."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "sign",
      "x": 56,
      "y": 6,
      "text": [
